27,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
28,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It seems we have a real problem with accountability; during the last outage, support was so fragmented that no one took ownership for two days. Also, capital requests are being trimmed while operating costs slide through.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings are concerning. Our yard hardware is a fragmented mix of old models, and a previous scheduling trial was abandoned for spreadsheets. Furthermore, our peak-season calendar allows no freeze window for cutovers.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,May,,"It's a bit of a mess, isn't it? Our dispatch tool is basically a fossil—we've skipped upgrades because we're too busy to test them. Plus, those separate add-on licenses are just bleeding us dry every year.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We are facing a critical staffing shortage. Half of our system administrators are retiring this year, and replacing them is taking nearly a year. We simply do not have the internal bandwidth to manage a complex transition.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we are in a delightful predicament. My research confirms May's suspicion; while the board ignores the creeping tide of operating expenses, those separate add-on licenses are indeed a financial leak that never seems to stop.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Misaki, that staffing shortage sounds very stressful. If we don't have the people to manage the transition, we might end up with the same lack of ownership I saw in the outage reports.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, the lack of ownership is a risk, but the physical reality is more immediate. If a system cannot be deployed without a freeze window, we risk a total collapse of dispatch during peak season.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, you're so dramatic! But you're right—if we're too scared to even test an upgrade, we're just waiting for the whole thing to crash. We need something that doesn't require a miracle to install.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, I agree. Beyond the installation, we must consider the training. My research shows that depot supervisors often abandon standard procedures if they are too rigid or poorly integrated into their daily routines.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, a system that is too rigid is indeed a liability. However, we must also ensure that the ""simplicity"" we seek doesn't come with a subscription fee that grows like a weed in the background.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I agree that costs are important, but I'm more worried about the governance. If we pick a system that is too complex for our remaining staff, we'll just end up with another fragmented support mess.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Misaki, the tendency of supervisors to revert to manual work is exactly what I saw with the 2021 trial. If the tool doesn't fit the yard's reality, it will be ignored.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, exactly! Why build a fancy digital palace if everyone just wants to live in their spreadsheets? We need a vendor who actually understands the chaos of a depot, not some theoretical perfection.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, that is a fair point. If the system is too theoretical, the burden of bridging the gap falls on the few administrators we have left, who are already stretched too thin.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a charming cycle, is it not? We seek a tool to reduce chaos, yet we risk hiring a vendor who charges us a premium for the privilege of managing that very chaos. We must prioritize a predictable cost structure.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I think we should look for a vendor that offers a single point of accountability. If we can avoid fragmented support and a rigid design, we might actually keep the plan aligned with our needs.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. However, accountability is useless if the software cannot survive our hardware. We must prioritize a vendor whose system is compatible with legacy devices and can be deployed without a total freeze.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm with you all, but let's not forget the ""fossil"" problem. We need a vendor who handles the heavy lifting of updates so we don't just skip them for a decade. No more patching holes!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. We need a solution that minimizes the burden on our staff. A vendor that provides comprehensive training and a flexible, intuitive interface will prevent our supervisors from reverting to manual work.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are all in agreement that we require a miracle worker. I shall support any candidate that offers a transparent, bundled pricing model and a low administrative burden, lest we pay for a ghost system.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
